WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:07.191
After three days of traveling, Miles and Edward reached Hendon Hall.

2
00:00:07.192 --> 00:00:12.839
"Welcome to Hendon Hall, my king," Miles said as they entered his old home.

3
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.309
"There are seventy rooms and thirty servants here.

4
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.151
Can you imagine that?"

5
00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:23.605
Edward thought of his palace with its hundreds of rooms and servants.

6
00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:27.993
"Actually, I can."

7
00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:32.509
"I've been away for ten years," Miles went on.

8
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:39.572
"But I'm sure my father, my brother Arthur, and Lady Edith will be overjoyed at my arrival.

9
00:00:39.573 --> 00:00:43.384
Don't be offended if they ignore you in their excitement at seeing me.

10
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:48.226
They'll soon welcome you into their home and their hearts."

11
00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:52.475
"And what about your other brother?" Edward asked.

12
00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:58.350
"The one who lied and said you were eloping with Lady Edith?"

13
00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:02.690
"Perhaps Hugh will be polite to us," Miles said quietly.

14
00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:07.156
"That's the best I can hope for."

15
00:01:07.157 --> 00:01:13.542
They entered a spacious room, where a man was writing letters at a table by the fireplace.

16
00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:19.576
"Sit there." Miles pointed Edward toward a chair and rushed over to the man.

17
00:01:19.577 --> 00:01:25.941
"Hello, Hugh, I'm back!" Miles said, smiling broadly.

18
00:01:25.942 --> 00:01:29.012
Edward was surprised that this man was Hugh.

19
00:01:29.013 --> 00:01:36.815
"Miles must be so happy to be home that he's even glad to see Hugh," Edward thought.

20
00:01:36.816 --> 00:01:39.485
Hugh shrank back from Miles.

21
00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:45.063
Slowly his stare changed from fear to curiosity to pity.

22
00:01:45.064 --> 00:01:51.105
"From the state of your clothes, poor stranger, the world has treated you harshly," Hugh said.

23
00:01:51.106 --> 00:01:56.249
"I have no idea who you are, and you've obviously mistaken me for someone else."

24
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.302
Miles shook his head in disbelief.

25
00:01:59.303 --> 00:02:06.390
"Are you saying that you don't recognize me, your own brother? Miles Hendon?"

26
00:02:06.391 --> 00:02:12.620
"Can you really be my lost brother?" Hugh's face lit up with surprise.

27
00:02:12.621 --> 00:02:16.621
"Let me get a good look at you."

28
00:02:16.622 --> 00:02:19.721
Hugh pulled Miles toward a window.

29
00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:25.907
Then Hugh looked Miles up and down, turned him this way and that, and studied him thoroughly.

30
00:02:25.908 --> 00:02:30.821
Meanwhile Miles laughed and chattered on.

31
00:02:30.822 --> 00:02:36.924
"Yes, it's your dear old Miles. Oh, this is a great day!

32
00:02:36.925 --> 00:02:41.049
Give me your hand, Hugh! Let me kiss your cheek!"

33
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:46.284
Miles was about to hug his brother, but Hugh raised a hand in protest.

34
00:02:46.285 --> 00:02:49.567
"I can't bear this disappointment."

35
00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:56.662
Stunned, Miles couldn't speak for a moment. "What disappointment?"

36
00:02:56.663 --> 00:02:59.410
Hugh shook his head sadly.

37
00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:06.090
"Perhaps others will notice something that I've missed, but I'm afraid the letter was correct."

38
00:03:06.091 --> 00:03:08.954
"What letter?"

39
00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:14.256
"A few years ago, we received a letter that Miles had died in battle."

40
00:03:14.257 --> 00:03:19.150
"Well, that's obviously not true!" Miles said angrily.

41
00:03:19.151 --> 00:03:23.979
"Call our father! He'll recognize me at once."

42
00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.668
"I can't summon the dead," Hugh said.

43
00:03:27.669 --> 00:03:33.255
"Our father is dead? Oh, this is terrible news indeed."

44
00:03:33.256 --> 00:03:37.645
Miles' voice trembled as he struggled to control himself.

45
00:03:37.646 --> 00:03:41.704
"Then let me see our brother, Arthur."

46
00:03:41.705 --> 00:03:44.472
"Arthur has also died."

47
00:03:44.473 --> 00:03:49.300
"Both of them gone! They were such good people."

48
00:03:49.301 --> 00:03:53.412
Miles stopped to wipe tears from his eyes.

49
00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:58.529
"Please don't tell me that Lady Edith has died too."

50
00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:03.453
"No, she still lives here," Hugh said.

51
00:04:03.454 --> 00:04:06.089
Miles heaved a sigh of relief.

52
00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:12.500
"Then bring her to me—and bring the old servants too."

53
00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.853
To Edward's surprise, Hugh nodded.

54
00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:23.294
"Only Margaret and David still work here," Hugh said, "but I'll get them."

55
00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:27.597
After Hugh left the room, Miles went over to Edward.

56
00:04:27.598 --> 00:04:33.679
"It's terrible when no one believes you're the person that you say you are."

57
00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.290
"I don't doubt that you are Miles Hendon," Edward said.

58
00:04:38.291 --> 00:04:41.582
"Do you doubt that I'm the king?"

59
00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:47.098
"Uh . . . um . . ." Miles was saved from replying by Hugh's return.

60
00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:53.220
The servants were with him, and a beautiful, sad woman walked slowly behind them.

61
00:04:53.221 --> 00:04:58.919
Her eyes were focused on the floor, and she was as pale as a ghost.

62
00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:05.647
Miles sprang toward her. "Oh, my darling Edith!"

63
00:05:05.648 --> 00:05:11.177
At the sound of Miles' voice, Edith blushed.

64
00:05:11.178 --> 00:05:15.834
Hugh waved Miles away and said to her, "Do you know him?"

65
00:05:15.835 --> 00:05:21.590
Trembling, Edith raised her head and looked into Miles' eyes.

66
00:05:21.591 --> 00:05:24.692
"I've never seen him before."

67
00:05:24.693 --> 00:05:31.245
With a moan and a stifled sob, she fled the room.

68
00:05:31.246 --> 00:05:35.784
"Edith!" Miles cried after her.

69
00:05:35.785 --> 00:05:42.668
Hugh grinned and asked the servants if they recognized Miles, but they shook their heads.

70
00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:48.125
"Well, the servants don't know you," Hugh said after he dismissed them.

71
00:05:48.126 --> 00:05:51.506
"And neither does my wife."

72
00:05:51.507 --> 00:05:57.615
"Your wife!" In an instant Miles was pinning Hugh to the wall.

73
00:05:57.616 --> 00:06:00.104
"I know what happened!

74
00:06:00.105 --> 00:06:06.402
You wrote that letter yourself, and then you stole the woman I love and everything that's mine."

75
00:06:06.403 --> 00:06:11.290
Hugh wiggled free from Miles' grasp and ran from the room.

76
00:06:11.291 --> 00:06:19.247
Edward jumped up. "This isn't exactly the welcome you were expecting. Should we leave?"

77
00:06:19.248 --> 00:06:27.143
Miles scowled. "Since my father and older brother are dead, I'm the rightful owner of Hendon Hall."

78
00:06:27.144 --> 00:06:30.337
He planted his feet firmly on the floor.

79
00:06:30.338 --> 00:06:36.258
"And I'm not going anywhere!"

